                <pb facs="0278" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg190"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay informs Mr. Conger that if sufficient guaranties of early action and
                    satisfactory conclusion of work are promptly secured, the proposals of the
                    Nanking viceroy regarding Whangpu conservancy are unobjectionable to this
                    Government.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
